bri"/><a:ea typeface="Calibri"/><a:cs typeface="Calibri"/><a:sym typeface="Calibri"/></a:rPr><a:t>Synthesis of Branches in Glycogen</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr/></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:cxnSp><p:nvCxnSpPr><p:cNvPr id="473" name="Google Shape;473;p64"/><p:cNvCxnSpPr/><p:nvPr/></p:nvCxnSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="457200" y="762000"/><a:ext cx="8229600" cy="0"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="straightConnector1"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/><a:ln cap="flat" cmpd="thinThick" w="57150"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="2FB0DC"/></a:solidFill><a:prstDash val="solid"/><a:miter lim="800000"/><a:headEnd len="med" w="med" type="none"/><a:tailEnd len="med" w="med" type="none"/></a:ln></p:spPr></p:cxnSp><p:pic><p:nvPicPr><p:cNvPr descr="An illustration of branch synthesis in glycogen.&#xA;In the first line, HO binds up to the first point on a hexagon with O at the third point of the hexagon. Next to that hexagon is a U with both sides touching hexagons. This U has O at the bottom, in the middle. This repeats six times to the right. It then repeats three more times, only the hexagons are filled in tan. To the right of that is a hexagon with O on the third point, and a half-U pointing to glycogen core in a purple oval. A dashed red arrow starts at the U before the first tan hexagon, and extends to the last hexagon. Below this line is an arrow, with &quot;glycogen-branching enzyme (in blue) to the left. This arrow points to another line of 6 hexagons and Us, as described above, and ends with a hexagon. On the fourth point of the hexagon (clockwise), it binds down to O, with a line extending down to the last hexagon in the third line. To the right of this, it states, (alpha1[right arrow]6) Branchpoint.&quot; The third line has three sets of the tan hexagons and Us, with the last hexagon not colored. To the right is a half-U, pointing to glycogen core in a purple oval. " id="474" name="Google Shape;474;p64"/><p:cNvPicPr preferRelativeResize="0"/><p:nvPr/></p:nvPicPr><p:blipFill rotWith